==Trivia==
* Dinh's bulwark is mentioned in the short story [[Transcript:Lab Notes|Lab Notes]] from the [[Kourend Chronicles]], in which [[Xamphur|the writer]] remarks that the bulwark was likely intended as a prototype of the [[Doors of Dinh]], but that the bulwark lacked something that allowed the Doors to properly seal away the [[Wintertodt]].{{CiteText|text=Transcript:Lab Notes{{!}}Lab Notes|quote=Before I sign off, there’s also the other matter you asked me to look into. I can confirm that the Bulwark of legend was among the artefacts abandoned in the tower – and if the rest of our contact’s information is solid, then I will also concede that it does indeed share some similarities with the Doors of Dinh. It’s my hypothesis that the Bulwark was intended as some kind of early prototype – but it’s missing some key factor that made the Doors fit for purpose, an issue I discovered quite by chance after freezing an assistant during testing.}}
* The special attack of Dinh's bulwark can be used to damage [[aviansie]]—which cannot be targeted by [[melee]] attacks directly—if used on a nearby ground NPC.
* Despite the special attack description stating that it can hit surrounding enemies in a 10 × 10 area, the actual range is 11 × 11. 
* The shield's animation will play when the wielder fails to block an incoming attack. This can alert the wielder to heal as it occurs prior to the hit landing.
* The design on the front of the shield is made to look like an eye, alongside an eye-blinking animation.

